<p>UK trades businesses, plumbers, electricians, HVAC engineers, are the backbone of the construction and maintenance economy. But running a trades business means wearing every hat: doing the work, quoting the jobs, ordering parts, scheduling the diary, and keeping customers happy. AI is helping trades businesses professionalise their operations without taking on more admin or more staff.</p>
<p>Generic AI tools don't understand trades. A generic chatbot can't diagnose a boiler fault. A generic document generator doesn't know what materials a typical bathroom refit requires. Generic scheduling tools don't understand that a parts run mid-job changes your whole day. They produce output that looks plausible but needs so much correction that you'd have been faster doing it yourself.</p>
<p>Bespoke AI solutions are trained on your trade and your business. We build quote generation that knows your material suppliers, your labour rates, and your typical job patterns. We create diagnostic assistants trained on the equipment types you actually work on, whether that's Worcester Bosch boilers or Daikin heat pumps. We implement scheduling that accounts for parts availability, traffic, and the reality that some jobs overrun whilst others finish early.</p>
<p>Compliance matters in the trades, particularly for gas and electrical work. AI can help track Gas Safe registration renewals, NICEIC assessment dates, and qualification expiry across your team. For customer-facing AI, we ensure all communication is professional and accurate, and that any AI-assisted advice is clearly framed as guidance rather than a substitute for a qualified engineer's assessment. Customer data is handled in accordance with UK GDPR.</p>
<p>We worked with a plumbing and heating business in the Midlands with four engineers. The owner was spending two evenings per week on quoting and customer follow-ups. Our AI quote generation tool, trained on their historical job data and supplier pricing, reduced quoting time from 40 minutes to 8 minutes per job, with a 22% increase in quote-to-job conversion rate attributed to faster response times. The scheduling optimisation tool increased average jobs per engineer per day from 4.5 to 5.3 by reducing travel time between sites. The owner reclaimed both evenings per week whilst the business grew turnover by 15% without adding staff.</p>

